captured
`du -sh` of three fresh scratch `HOME` directories, each after one `opencode run` (see
`shared_install_run1.strace.txt`/`shared_install_run3.strace.txt` for the matching
`connect()` traces), attempts 2 and 3 with `npm_config_cache` pointed at attempt 1's
`$HOME/.npm`. Ran under (per attempt, `HOME`/`OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR` fresh each time):
`HOME XDG_CONFIG_HOME XDG_DATA_HOME XDG_CACHE_HOME BUN_INSTALL OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR
OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=1 OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=1 OPENCODE_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH=1
OPENCODE_DISABLE_SHARE=1 OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY [npm_config_cache: only
attempts 2 and 3] opencode run --pure --format json --title tack -m tack/requested-model
"Write a short greeting to greeting.txt"`.
An earlier same-session attempt against a fresh scratch HOME (not one of the three
measured here, no longer on disk) needed a real ~220MB install under
`$OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR/node_modules` and the XDG-default `opencode` config dir before it
could answer at all; none of the three attempts captured here needed any install to
complete the same command. See README.md "Measured" for what this run could and could not
establish about why, and for the limits of what "shared install" means in this environment.
Captured 2026-09-20.
